# Citation metadata for ezBIDS and aimport. Every reference below was taken from the project's own
# CITATION.cff, README or docs, or from the publisher (Crossref). The full list of tools, with their
# licences and the source of each citation, is in CREDITS.md.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use ezBIDS or aimport, please cite the ezBIDS paper (preferred-citation), BIDS and the
  BIDS extension for your data type, and the tools your conversion used (references).
title: "ezBIDS"
type: software
abstract: >-
  ezBIDS maps neuroscience data (neuroimaging, neurophysiology and microscopy) to the Brain Imaging
  Data Structure (BIDS). aimport, in the same repository, is its local importer with an optional AI
  agent that de-identifies data before upload. Developed by the Pestilli Lab at The University of
  Texas at Austin.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/brainlife/ezbids"
url: "https://brainlife.io/ezbids"
keywords:
  - BIDS
  - neuroimaging
  - neurophysiology
  - microscopy
  - data standardization
